{
  "requirement": "Every source text the harness supplies to a model, including mandatory inputs,\n`habeas` reads, and `ripgrep` results, and every source text Habeas displays in\nthe book or `habeas info`, MUST be redacted:\n\n1. In a workspace `habeas.toml` or user configuration file, the value of every\n   explicit credential field defined by {cite}`requirements.authoring.credentials`\n   MUST be replaced. Such a file that is not valid TOML MUST be replaced whole,\n   with `configuration` as the kind, because its fields cannot be located.\n2. In every source, each match of a built-in rule of the `secretshape` crate MUST\n   be replaced. The replaced region MUST be extended through each adjacent region\n   that the crate's entropy heuristic flags and that only whitespace separates\n   from the region, repeating until no flagged region is adjacent. The heuristic\n   MUST NOT cause redaction on its own.\n\nA replacement MUST read `[REDACTED:<kind>]`, where `<kind>` is the credential\nfield or the rule's name, and MUST keep every line break within the replaced\ntext, so line numbers are unchanged. Outlines MUST be built from the original\nsource, and the structural hash MUST hash each text piece that overlaps a\nredacted region in its redacted form, so evidence never depends on a credential's\nvalue and redaction never changes or breaks a file's outline. The `secretshape` version MUST be pinned exactly; upgrading\nit MAY change redaction and hashes and MUST be treated as a deliberate change.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no unmet obligation and no untested one in the requirement's text. I did not verify the `secretshape` scanning itself, only how the code uses it.\n\n**Surfaces that must be redacted**\n- **Mandatory inputs, `habeas` reads and `ripgrep` results.**\n  - Outline inputs come from `OutlineCache::parse` (src/inputs.rs). It builds `Redaction::of_file`, parses the outline from the original source, and stores `redaction.apply(&source)`.\n  - `ParsedSource::node_range` and `InputSelector::resolve` emit only that redacted text.\n  - Requirement, example and term inputs go through `redact_lines`.\n  - `read_lines`, `read_selector` and `search` all use `source_input` or `resolve`, so line-range reads, item reads and search results are redacted. Search matches against the original text, but the results it returns are redacted.\n- **Prompts.** `initial_prompt` serializes those mandatory inputs. Citation commentary is redacted in `model_citations_value` (src/citations.rs).\n- **Book and `habeas info`.**\n  - `render_detail_sections` redacts the requirement text, the validation findings and an unreadable record.\n  - `render_input` shows resolved, redacted text, or redacts the recorded text.\n  - `info_markdown` reuses the same rendering.\n\n**Per-obligation mapping**\n- **Credential fields (item 1).** `credential_fields`, `item_fields` and `value_fields` locate every value under `authoring.configs.*.credentials` and `api_key`, including inline tables and multi-line strings. `is_configuration_file(_for)` picks `habeas.toml` files and the user config file, including aliases. `configuration_regions` replaces a file that is not valid TOML whole, with kind `configuration`.\n  - Tests: `configuration_credential_fields_are_redacted_by_name_whatever_their_values`, `invalid_configuration_files_are_redacted_whole_keeping_lines`, `the_user_configuration_file_and_its_aliases_are_configuration_files`.\n- **Rule matches and extension (item 2).** `secret_regions` scans with the rule-only scanner, then extends each region forward and backward through adjacent heuristic-flagged tokens separated only by whitespace. Heuristic findings alone never start a region. `scanners` removes the input cap, and `merge` joins overlaps.\n  - Tests: `private_keys_are_redacted_from_header_through_body_keeping_lines` (forward extension), `regions_extend_backward_keep_crlf_and_scan_past_a_mebibyte` (backward extension and large input), `heuristic_findings_alone_are_not_redacted`, `tokens_in_code_are_redacted_without_adjacent_code`.\n- **Replacement format and line breaks.** `Redaction::slice` writes `[REDACTED:<kind>]` plus the region's line breaks, including `\\r\\n`, via `push_line_breaks`.\n  - Tests: the same redaction tests, plus `slices_concatenate_to_the_redacted_whole`, which checks line counts and slice concatenation.\n- **Outlines and hashes.**\n  - `parse_redacted`, `plain_text` and `Builder::piece` (src/outline/mod.rs) build the outline from the original source and hash each text piece in its redacted form.\n  - Tests: `redaction_never_changes_an_outline` (structure identical across YAML, Rust, TOML, Markdown and plain text) and `hashes_do_not_depend_on_credential_values`. The latter also checks that hashes still change when text outside a redacted region changes.\n- **Pinned version.** Cargo.toml has `secretshape = \"=0.1.0\"` with a comment saying that a new version may change redaction and hashes. This is declarative, with no conditional or transformation.\n\n**End-to-end tests**\n- `model_inputs_reads_searches_and_citation_prompts_are_redacted` (src/authoring/tools.rs) covers mandatory inputs, prompts, `habeas` reads of the config file and of a line range, `ripgrep` including a pattern that matches the credential, and citation commentary.\n- `detail_pages_and_info_display_redacted_source` (src/index.rs) covers the detail page and `habeas info`.\n\n**Unspecified behavior and unacknowledged gaps**\n- I found no unspecified behavior and no unmarked implementation or test. The `{impl}` and `{test}` markings are present on the relevant items. No `{fixme}` references are involved.",
  "references": "ca6fd37670d978dfa4182c63040bf0c41597afeb42d41d6abf21d65c136c1489",
